      "name": "Question 4",
      "problem": "If ${({y}^{4})}^{-2}={y}^{k},$ then $k=$",
      "worked_solution": "We multiply the exponents, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{({y}^{4})}^{-2} & = \\\\ {y}^{4\\cdot (-2)} & = \\\\ {y}^{-8}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, $k=-8.$",
